ure from strategy: main_budget_by_case; Missing required figure from strategy: controls_permutation; paper.tex references figure missing from figure_manifest.json: figures/protocol_overview.png; paper.tex references figure missing from figure_manifest.json: figures/main_budget_by_case.pdf; paper.tex references figure missing from figure_manifest.json: figures/controls_permutation.pdf\n\n## Supplementary Information validation\n- appendix_present: `True`\n- heading_present: `True`\n- placed_after_references: `True`\n- pre_bibliography_clearpage_present: `True`\n- clearpage_present: `True`\n- visible_character_count: `7575`\n- substantive_element_count: `10`\n- rendered_checked: `False`\n- rendered_heading_present: `False`\n- rendered_visible_character_count: `0`\n\n## Evidence validation\n- bundle_path: `work/results/t06/claude/20261111_064241/paper/scientific-evidence`\n- bundle_present: `True`\n- verification_report: `work/results/t06/claude/20261111_064241/paper/scientific-evidence/verification-report.json`\n- total_references: `68`\n- resolved_references: `23`\n- anchored_references: `45`\n- dangling_references: `0`\n- manifests_checked: `6`\n\n## Agentic evidence audit\n- checked: `True`\n- verdict: `fail`\n- finding_count: `4`\n- summary: Reported numbers, qualification wording, and the search-versus-final separation match the evidence. Four protocol, provenance and implementation statements are ungrounded or contradicted by the staged source.\n\n### Audit findings to fix\n- `protocol-definitions-ungrounded-1` (Problem Setup and Method (Sec. 3.1, Eq. 1)): The evaluator source is not staged, so these definitions cannot be checked against any artifact. The candidate source takes `ridge`, `hi` and `lo` from the request, so it does not show the value 0.01 or how the mid pair is chosen. Only the Research-question paragraph hedges (\"as defined by the task's metric\"); Sec. 3.1 states them as fact.\n  - claim: Ridge lambda=0.01 in Eq. (1), plus \"The top pair is ranks 1 and 2 of the full-table fit; the mid pair is ranks floor(M/2) and floor(M/2)+1\", stated as the definition used.\n  - evidence: source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py lines 20-24 and 238-240 (ridge, hi, lo are request fields); claims_grounding.json has no claim for lambda=0.01 or the mid-rank rule; the only mention of \"ridge 0.01\" is in paper_strategy.md, which is not an evidence source.\n  - requested_fix: State that lambda=0.01 and the top/mid pair rule are taken from the task description and could not be verified against evaluator source, or drop them. Keep the wording consistent with the \"as we understand it\" caveats used elsewhere.\n- `dataset-provenance-ungrounded-1` (Supplementary Information, Data provenance (Table tab:prov)): No artifact in the evidence trail contains these commits or licences. claims_grounding.json has no claim for them, and the brief itself is not among the staged artifacts. They are visible Supplementary Information claims with no support.\n  - claim: Dataset repositories, commit hashes (18c29834, 6322995a, f7d2896d, 4c1ff5e3) and licences (apache-2.0, cc-by-4.0, CC-BY-4.0), attributed to \"the public task brief\".\n  - evidence: claims_grounding.json (no claim or source id covers dataset versions or licences); derived/task_meta/final_meta.json and search_meta.json record only row and model counts; paper.tex Table tab:prov.\n  - requested_fix: Remove the commit and licence columns, or mark them explicitly as unverified, transcribed values with no artifact support. Keep only the grounded row and model counts.\n- `warm-start-source-mismatch-1` (Supplementary Information, Algorithmic specification of the studied configuration): The staged source does not warm-start every fit. `verify_by_refit` defaults to the full-table `ctx[\"theta0\"]` when no `theta_start` is passed. Every probe in `_min_prefix`, and the refit at the start of each polish round, therefore starts from the full-table fit. Only the re-linearised loop in `_relinearize` passes the previous theta.\n  - claim: All fits are warm-started from the previous solution.\n  - evidence: source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py line 137-138 (`ctx[\"theta0\"] if theta_start is None`), lines 161 and 204 (calls without theta_start), line 193 (call with theta).\n  - requested_fix: Change to \"refits inside the re-linearised greedy loop are warm-started from the previous solution; prefix-bisection probes and polish refits start from the full-table fit\", or delete the sentence.\n- `llm-usage-overclaim-1` (Supplementary Information, LLM Usage): The sentence conflicts with the manuscript itself and with the artifacts. The protocol-overview figure is a schematic with no derived content, as the Data provenance subsection says. Table tab:data takes its development sizes from the copied meta JSON files, and Table tab:prov comes from a task brief that is not staged. The pipeline narrative, including the claim about who proposed configurations, has no entry in claims_grounding.json.\n  - claim: Every figure and table in this paper is derived by script from the evaluator's recorded outputs. The assistant \"proposed configurations, ran a development evaluation, froze one selection\".\n  - evidence: paper.tex Data provenance paragraph (\"Figure fig:overview is a schematic with no quantitative content\"); figure_manifest.json protocol_overview with source_ids []; claims_grounding.json (no claim for the pipeline description); derived/task_meta/*.json.\n  - requested_fix: Narrow to \"the quantitative figures and the case, aggregate and development-score tables are derived by script from the recorded evaluator outputs\". Remove or soften the unsupported statements about how configurations were proposed and the pipeline's order of steps.\n# Draft reference gap analysis\n\n**Status:** ready. Three targeted retrieval targets.\n\nCoverage of Bradley–Terry theory (extensions, existence/consistency, uncertainty) is dense. The existing bibliography does not cover three areas the draft relies on or motivates itself with. The draft concedes this in its \"Scope of the bibliography\" paragraph and in the Extended limitations. Numeric claims are grounded in `paper_data.json` and are not targets.\n\n## Missing literatures\n- Chatbot Arena / MT-Bench pairwise LLM evaluation and the datasets used\n- Influence functions and leave-one-out / Cook's-distance-style deletion diagnostics\n- Manipulation and rigging of crowd-vote or pairwise-comparison rankings\n\n## Targets\n\n1. **arena-leaderboard-context** (Introduction, high, benchmark_context)\n   - Anchor: \"Leaderboards that aggregate 'which of A and B is better' judgments into Bradley–Terry (BT) ratings are used to choose models…\"\n   - Reason: The motivating claim about leaderboard use has no citation. The Data section uses Arena 55k/140k and MT-Bench human judgments without citing the platform or dataset papers.\n   - Search topics: Chatbot Arena platform paper; MT-Bench human judgments / LLM-as-a-judge; Arena human-preference dataset.\n\n2. **influence-deletion-method** (Problem Setup and Method, high, background)\n   - Anchor: \"Deleting row $i$ perturbs the stationarity condition by $-\\nabla\\ell_i$, so a Newton step predicts the change of the gap…\"\n   - Reason: The first-order influence formula with leverage correction is the core of the studied configuration and the basis of the B2 comparator. It has no citation to influence-function or case-deletion literature. Only Broderick et al. is cited.\n   - Search topics: influence functions for black-box predictions; Cook's distance / case deletion in logistic regression; one-step leave-one-out approximations for M-estimators.\n\n3. **manipulation-positioning** (Related Work, medium, positioning)\n   - Anchor: \"Work on adversarial manipulation of crowd-vote leaderboards, on evaluation practices of arena-style platforms, and on influence functions…\"\n   - Reason: The draft motivates the removal budget through deliberate action and rigging, then disclaims any positioning against that work. One or two citations would replace the disclaimer.\n   - Search topics: adversarial vote manipulation of LLM arena leaderboards; robustness of pairwise-comparison rankings to corrupted comparisons.\n\n## Not targeted\nRelated-work paragraphs on BT extensions, estimation and uncertainty are well supported. Adding more there would only grow the bibliography.\npostdraft_citation_weave_agent_claude_20261111_075327.log\npostdraft_citation_weave_prompt.md\npostdraft_reference_query_plan.json\npostdraft_reference_query_plan.md\npostdraft_reference_query_plan_agent_claude_20261111_075327.log\npostdraft_reference_query_plan_prompt.md\npostdraft_reference_query_plan_validation_feedback.json\npostdraft_reference_query_plan_validation_feedback.md\npostdraft_reference_retrieval.log\npostdraft_references.bib\npostdraft_references_provenance.json","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
