{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvrTTgq4x9tPdX88V9Ui","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018UoJ7xe2QEmT3Ma7W4AU7R","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'E'\nimport re\ns=open('paper.tex').read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s,a[:50]\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"Under a BT refit as defined by the task's metric (ridge $0.01$, ties as half wins)\",\"Under a BT refit as defined by the task's metric (a ridge-penalised fit with ties as half wins; the penalty value we use below is the one we understand the task to specify)\")\nrep(r\"\\qquad \\lambda=0.01,\",r\"\\qquad \\lambda=0.01\\ \\text{(as we understand the task's metric)},\")\nrep(r\"Two kinds of target are used. The \\emph{top} pair is ranks 1 and 2 of the full-table fit; the \\emph{mid} pair is ranks $\\lfloor M/2\\rfloor$ and $\\lfloor M/2\\rfloor+1$.\",\n r\"Two kinds of target are used: a \\emph{top} pair and a \\emph{mid} pair of adjacent ranks in the full-table fit. We take the top pair to be ranks 1 and 2 and the mid pair to be ranks $\\lfloor M/2\\rfloor$ and $\\lfloor M/2\\rfloor+1$; this rule, like the value of $\\lambda$ above, is our reading of the task description and could not be checked against evaluator source, which is not staged.\")\nrep(\"Dataset commits and licences come from the public task brief and are listed in the Supplement. \",\"Dataset versions and licences are not recorded in the evidence we hold and are therefore not reported here. \")\nrep(\"All fits are warm-started from the previous solution.\",\"Refits inside the re-linearised greedy loop are warm-started from the previous solution; prefix-bisection probes and polish refits start from the full-table fit.\")\nrep(\"Dataset versions and licences, from the public task brief, are in Table~\\\\ref{tab:prov}. Raw data are not redistributed.\",\"Raw data are not redistributed, and we do not report dataset commits or licences because no staged artifact records them; readers should take these from the dataset hosts.\")\n# remove table\ns=re.sub(r\"\\\\begin\\{table\\}\\[h\\]\\n\\\\centering\\n\\\\caption\\{Dataset versions and licences.*?\\\\end\\{table\\}\\n\\n?\",\"\",s,flags=re.S)\nrep(\"Every figure and table in this paper is derived by script from the evaluator's recorded outputs.\",\"The quantitative figures and the case, aggregate and development-score tables are derived by script from the recorded evaluator outputs.\")\nrep(\"with an LLM-based research assistant operating inside an automated pipeline that proposed configurations, ran a development evaluation, froze one selection, and then ran a sealed held-out evaluation whose results the manuscript reports.\",\"with an LLM-based research assistant operating inside an automated pipeline; the manuscript reports the recorded development scores and the recorded held-out evaluation of one frozen selection.\")\nopen('paper.tex','w').write(s)\nE\ngrep -n 'tab:prov\\|licen\\|commit' paper.tex claims_grounding.json | head"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2134,"cache_read_input_tokens":53599,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2134},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e5d3c29-1d53-44fb-9026-ca86d535f836","uuid":"7becb194-3b84-49c0-8c23-dd06240eb5cb","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:50:04.134Z","request_id":"req_011CgvrTT6sERWadMzicDLrN"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018UoJ7xe2QEmT3Ma7W4AU7R","type":"tool_result","content":"paper.tex:100:Table~\\ref{tab:data} lists the tables. The search procedure receives rows as integer participant indices with a coded outcome; names are not visible to it in the inspected candidate source. The held-out crowd table is the Chatbot Arena 140k preference release (data from the platform of \\citealp{https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2403.04132}) after content-hash deduplication against the development tables: from 135,634 raw rows, 2 were removed for content overlap with development data (a further 652 rows are listed in the evaluator metadata as prompt-only overlaps and were kept) and 2 rows of participants with fewer than 100 rows were dropped, leaving 135,630 rows over 52 models. The sports table holds NBA game results from 2006 to 2015 with 12,900 comparisons over 30 teams. The development tables are the Chatbot Arena 55k release (57,477 rows, 64 models) and the MT-Bench human-judgment table (3,355 rows, 6 models), the latter standing in for expert annotation. Dataset versions and licences are not recorded in the evidence we hold and are therefore not reported here. Model-judge data were not used.\npaper.tex:297:Raw data are not redistributed, and we do not report dataset commits or licences because no staged artifact records them; readers should take these from the dataset hosts. The held-out tables are prepared by the evaluator; the evaluator metadata records the content-overlap removals and prompt-only overlaps reported in Section~\\ref{sec:data}, and we have no further documentation of its preparation or checking procedure. The figures are built by \\texttt{scripts/derive\\_final\\_stats.py} (derived percentages and ratios from the evaluator's recorded episodes) and \\texttt{scripts/build\\_figures.py} (Figures~\\ref{fig:main} and~\\ref{fig:controls}); Figure~\\ref{fig:overview} is a schematic with no quantitative content. Tables~\\ref{tab:cases} and~\\ref{tab:full} are filled from \\texttt{derived/final\\_stats.json}. The seeds are 11 and 12 (development) and 21 and 22 (held-out); The recorded held-out evaluation episodes of the studied configuration took 4.45 s and 4.51 s each; the hardware is not recorded. We were not able to give independent timing for a full reproduction from raw data.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e5d3c29-1d53-44fb-9026-ca86d535f836","uuid":"28aa08b5-0a24-4557-a2e3-b4a505215ca8","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:50:04.208Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"paper.tex:100:Table~\\ref{tab:data} lists the tables. The search procedure receives rows as integer participant indices with a coded outcome; names are not visible to it in the inspected candidate source. The held-out crowd table is the Chatbot Arena 140k preference release (data from the platform of \\citealp{https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2403.04132}) after content-hash deduplication against the development tables: from 135,634 raw rows, 2 were removed for content overlap with development data (a further 652 rows are listed in the evaluator metadata as prompt-only overlaps and were kept) and 2 rows of participants with fewer than 100 rows were dropped, leaving 135,630 rows over 52 models. The sports table holds NBA game results from 2006 to 2015 with 12,900 comparisons over 30 teams. The development tables are the Chatbot Arena 55k release (57,477 rows, 64 models) and the MT-Bench human-judgment table (3,355 rows, 6 models), the latter standing in for expert annotation. Dataset versions and licences are not recorded in the evidence we hold and are therefore not reported here. Model-judge data were not used.\npaper.tex:297:Raw data are not redistributed, and we do not report dataset commits or licences because no staged artifact records them; readers should take these from the dataset hosts. The held-out tables are prepared by the evaluator; the evaluator metadata records the content-ov